# oasdiff breaking-change ALLOWLIST — deliberate breaks only.
#
# Passed to `oasdiff breaking` via --err-ignore. Any breaking change NOT listed here
# fails CI. Listing one is an explicit, reviewed act: a break must be CHOSEN, not
# discovered by a client (ADR-0002).
#
#   NOTE: ADR-0002 names this file `.oasdiff.yaml`. That was written before the tool's
#   interface was checked — oasdiff has no YAML allowlist format. The mechanism the ADR
#   mandates (a reviewed allowlist gating deliberate breaks) is unchanged; only the
#   filename and syntax differ. Recorded in docs/notes/contract-pioneer-log.md.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT — verified 2026-08-09 against oasdiff v1.28.0. Do not guess at this.
#
# One line per (METHOD, PATH, MESSAGE) triple, all lowercased. oasdiff suppresses a
# breaking change only when an ignore line contains ALL THREE of the method, the path,
# and the change text.
#
#   A line carrying the printed message ALONE matches nothing. It does not error —
#   it silently fails to suppress, and the gate stays red with no explanation.
#
# To derive a line, run the diff and read the two indented lines of the error:
#
#   error   [response-required-property-removed] at openapi.yaml
#           in API GET /users/profile                                     <- method + path
#             removed the required property `displayName` from the ...    <- message
#
# Concatenate them and lowercase the result:
#
#   in api get /users/profile removed the required property `displayname` from the ...
#
# A break affecting two operations needs TWO lines — one per operation.
#
# A WORKING EXAMPLE, exercised against real fixtures, lives at
# contract-fixtures/oasdiff-allowlist.txt. Copy its shape, not oasdiff's output.
#
# EVERY ENTRY MUST CARRY: the FS or ADR that authorised the break, and why.
# An entry with no reason is a bug, not an allowance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (empty — and correctly so)
#
# An earlier revision of this file predicted two entries would be needed once FS-0002
# serialized the profile endpoints: the success-envelope removal and the error-body
# change to problem+json. Those slices have now shipped and NEITHER entry is required.
#
# oasdiff compares openapi.yaml against its OWN previous revision. Both of those breaks
# are relative to the legacy swaggo document (docs/swagger.json) — a different file, in a
# different OpenAPI version, that oasdiff never sees. They are CROSS-DOCUMENT breaks and
# plane-1 breaking detection is structurally blind to them.
#
#   Consequence worth internalising: under serialize-on-touch, an endpoint's FIRST
#   serialization is the one change this gate cannot check. The ratchet guards every
#   revision AFTER the spec first lands on the base branch. Slice ⓪ is verified by
#   review and by the before/after behavioural checks in its FS — not by oasdiff.
#
# An allowlist entry that matches nothing is worse than no entry: it looks like coverage
# and silently rots. Add entries only when a real diff produces a real error message.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
